{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>You shall make it on the day of the atonements</b> — for the purpose of the atonements, to make atonement upon the altar for all foreignness and abomination. And in the Midrash Torat Kohanim (Tzav 1:15) it says that atonement for the altar was necessary lest a person contributed something stolen toward the work of the Tabernacle and the altar. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 29:36). But the correct interpretation is that 'upon the atonements' refers to the two rams, which serve as atonements for Aaron and his sons, as it says here (Exodus 29:33), 'And they shall eat them, with which atonement was made,' and even though the sin-offering is itself an atonement, and it is written, 'As has been done this day, so YHWH has commanded to do, to make atonement for you' (Leviticus 8:34) — according to the words of R. Abraham ibn Ezra (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 29:36)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The phrase הַכִּפֻּרִים in this verse is pointed by Ramban with the definite article plus plural, hence 'the atonements'; I have preserved his exact grammatical reading throughout."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:11.701909525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}